---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import Section from "../../components/Section.astro";
import Stage from "../../components/Stage.astro";
---
<Base title="Megamenu" description="iVOLT megamenu: a navigation bar whose items open wide panels with link groups and cards, working on hover and focus without JavaScript, and with intentional hover, keyboard, an overlay and a mobile accordion when JavaScript runs.">
  <article class="docs-prose">
    <h1>Megamenu</h1>
    <p>A navigation bar where an item can open a wide panel: groups of links, cards with art and counts, and a bottom bar with actions. The server sends links and panels; without JavaScript the panels open on hover and focus on large screens and sit open inline on small ones. On <code>init</code> the toggles appear, hover becomes intentional (short open and close delays), the keyboard gets arrows and Escape, an overlay dims the page and closed panels become inert. Below the <code>staticFrom</code> breakpoint the panels turn into an accordion.</p>
    <p class="docs-meta"><strong>CSS:</strong> <code>css/components/megamenu.css</code> (in <code>ivolt.css</code>). <strong>JS:</strong> <code>@intervolutions/ivolt/megamenu</code> or <code>auto.js</code>. Added in v0.4.</p>
    <Stage primary name="megamenu/basic" title="Wide panels from a bar" minHeight="34rem" />
    <Section title="Full-width panel with glass" num={1} lead={`iv-megamenu--full stretches the panel from edge to edge of the bar; add iv-glass to a panel to blur what sits behind it.`}>
      <Stage name="megamenu/full" title="Full-width panel with glass" minHeight="34rem" />
    </Section>

    <Section title="Options" num={2}>
      <div class="docs-scroller">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Attribute</th><th>Default</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>hover</code></td><td><code>data-iv-hover</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Open on intentional hover with fine pointers; <code>false</code> opens only on click and keyboard.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>openDelay</code>, <code>closeDelay</code></td><td><code>data-iv-open-delay</code>, <code>data-iv-close-delay</code></td><td><code>120</code>, <code>200</code></td><td>Milliseconds before a hover opens or closes a panel.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>staticFrom</code></td><td><code>data-iv-static-from</code></td><td><code>lg</code></td><td>Breakpoint from which panels float; below it they behave as an accordion.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>overlay</code></td><td><code>data-iv-overlay</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Dim the page behind an open panel.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>closeOthers</code></td><td><code>data-iv-close-others</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Opening an item closes the others.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Methods and events" num={3} lead={`open(itemOrIndex), close(), toggle(item), destroy(); read openItem. Events on the root: iv:open/iv:close (cancelable) then iv:opened/iv:closed, with detail.item and a reason.`}>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Keyboard and assistive technology" num={4}>
      <p>Tab reaches links and toggles in order; Enter, Space or Down on a toggle opens its panel and Left and Right move between toggles, Home and End jump. Escape closes and returns focus to the toggle; Tab out of a panel closes it. Toggles carry <code>aria-expanded</code> and <code>aria-controls</code>; closed panels are inert. The links stay plain links, so no menu roles are used.</p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Without JavaScript" num={5} lead={`Each link navigates. On large screens a panel shows while its item is hovered or focused; on small screens the panels are open inline under their links. The toggles are hidden.`}>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Common mistakes" num={6}>
      <ul>
        <li>Putting essential links only inside panels: the item link itself should lead to the section.</li>
        <li>More than five or six items: a megamenu is wide; consider a sidebar or a search.</li>
        <li>Very tall panels: keep them under the viewport height or they will scroll internally.</li>
      </ul>
    </Section>
  </article>
</Base>
